 "segments": [
  "[  0.00-  4.98] He put a bronze ball in a dragon's mouth and told the emperor, if this ever falls out, run!",
  "[  5.30- 10.06] The whole court burst out laughing. You see, there were eight dragons coiled around a giant",
  "[ 10.06- 15.00] bronze jar, each holding a ball over a frog's open mouth. But the emperor had the biggest army",
  "[ 15.00- 19.72] in the world, and he wasn't about to run from a jar. Weeks later, a ball fell, but nothing",
  "[ 19.72- 24.56] happened. Not even a ripple in the emperor's wine. Now they laughed even harder. The emperor",
  "[ 24.56- 28.46] called it the world's most expensive toy and threw the inventor out of the city,",
  "[ 28.46- 32.64] jar and all. So he dragged it up a hill outside the walls and lived there alone.",
  "[ 32.86- 38.22] Then, one night, a ball dropped. Then another. Then all ate at once. He ran to the city gates,",
  "[ 38.36- 43.28] screaming for everyone to get out. Hey, it's the toy guy! Did your frogs get hungry again?",
  "[ 43.50- 47.38] The guards laughed him all the way back up the hill. The next morning, the palace was",
  "[ 47.38- 52.24] a pile of rubble. Inside the jar hung a heavy pendulum, with a rod pointing at each dragon.",
  "[ 52.46- 56.48] The slightest nudge, and the pendulum swung into a rod, the rod snapped the dragon's",
  "[ 56.48- 60.14] jaw open, and the ball dropped. One ball meant a nudge from far away.",
  "[ 60.38- 64.78] All eight meant the biggest earthquake the empire had ever seen was right underneath them."
 ],
